          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What standards guide electronics recycling projects?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "NIST SP 800-88, HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312, and California's electronic waste rules provide relevant reference points for equipment handling and data-bearing media. The appropriate process depends on equipment type, data risk, volume, and the customer's internal policies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS serves Bakersfield, Kern County, and organizations across the San Joaquin Valley through scheduled commercial pickup. Service planning can include offices, campuses, healthcare operations, agricultural facilities, distribution environments, and public agencies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup timing depends on volume, equipment preparation, loading conditions, and route availability. Contact STS with your preferred window and project details to discuss same-week scheduling when available. Project planning is based on the equipment mix and site requirements rather than a standard appointment length."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is available at no cost for qualifying volumes and project conditions. STS reviews the equipment mix, estimated volume, access requirements, and destination before confirming the service plan. Customers can provide equipment details by phone or email before scheduling."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment is received, documented, and routed according to its condition, data requirements, and material composition. Customers can request reporting that summarizes the project and supports internal asset records."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you handle a large equipment project?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS supports projects ranging from office clearouts to multi-site equipment refreshes, with planning for inventory, loading, transportation, and reporting. Share the estimated scope so the team can recommend an appropriate workflow for the Bakersfield project."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What electronics does STS recycle in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS accepts workplace technology, school equipment, medical electronics, and retired infrastructure through coordinated commercial pickup. Bakersfield organizations can consolidate computers, laptops, servers, monitors, printers, mobile devices, networking equipment, and accessories for one documented project."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does commercial electronics recycling work?",
